==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gmh|de}} {{m|gmh|velt}}, from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|feld}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*felþą}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*pelh₂-}}. Cognates include Dutch {{m|nl|veld}} and English {{m|en|field}}.<ref>{{R:EWddS|ed=22|hw=Feld}}</ref>. German {{m|de|Gefilde||fields}} is a collective derivation of ''Feld''.<ref>{{R:EWddS|ed=22|hw=Gefilde}}</ref>

